---
name: context-md-management
description: Create, edit, or review CONTEXT.md files and source-code directories using the user's hierarchical context-file rules.
---
# CONTEXT.md Management
Before creating, editing, or reviewing a `CONTEXT.md` file, or before creating a source-code directory, read [the context-file rules](references/context-md-management.md) in full and apply every applicable rule.
# Directory Context: `/packages/auxiliary`
## Purpose
The packages that are useful for the application Heidrun, but are not the application itself: a library and the public website. A package that is only a tool for the developers of Heidrun goes in `packages/dev_tools`.
## Key Exports & Entry Points
- `raw_coding_agent_cli/`: a library and a command line tool that send one prompt to `codex` or `claude`. See its own CONTEXT.md.
- `website_public/`: the public website and documentation, built with VitePress. See its own CONTEXT.md.
## Rules
- A package that produces the application goes in `packages/apps`, never here.
- A package that is only a tool for the developers of Heidrun goes in `packages/dev_tools`, never here.
- No package in `packages/apps` imports a package from this folder.
- No package in this folder imports a package from `packages/dev_tools`.
## Background
- The folder `packages` was split into `apps` and `auxiliary` in [issue #120](https://github.com/heidrun-org/heidrun/issues/120).
- The development tools left this folder for `packages/dev_tools` in [issue #226](https://github.com/heidrun-org/heidrun/issues/226).
# Directory Context: `/packages/auxiliary/website_public`
## Purpose
The public website of Heidrun: a homepage and the user documentation, built with VitePress and published on GitHub Pages with the script `ghpage:deploy`.
## Key Exports & Entry Points
- `docs/`: the Markdown source of the website. `docs/index.md` is the homepage. `docs/documentation/` holds the documentation pages.
- `docs/.vitepress/config.ts`: the VitePress configuration (title, description, navigation, sidebar, `base`). It also writes the hero of the homepage from `data/identity.json`.
- `docs/public/favicon.svg`: the favicon of every page, linked by the `head` option of `docs/.vitepress/config.ts`.
- `tests/`: the Vitest tests of the website (configuration, pages, shortcuts page, identity texts, splash image, favicon, complete build).
- Command to run this folder: `pnpm --filter website_public dev`
- Command to test this folder: `pnpm --filter website_public test`
## Rules
- The `base` option in `docs/.vitepress/config.ts` equals the GitHub Pages path of the repository (`/heidrun/`).
- Nothing in this folder imports from another package of the workspace. The one shared file is `data/identity.json`, which is not a package.
- The title, the description, and the hero of the homepage come from `data/identity.json`. No page holds a hand-written copy.
- `docs/public/favicon.svg` is a copy of `data/images/heidrun_favicon.svg`, the favicon of the application, and the test `tests/favicon.test.ts` fails when the two files differ.
- The page `docs/documentation/shortcuts.md` is generated by `pnpm docs:shortcuts`: its text has no raw angle bracket, because VitePress reads `<agent>` as a Vue tag and the build fails.
- Every page of `docs/documentation/` except `shortcuts.md` is written by a coding agent with `pnpm docs:update_by_ai`, has the mark `<!-- generated by docs:update_by_ai -->`, and is never edited by hand. The rules are in `packages/dev_tools/documentation_updater/CONTEXT.md`. The file `docs/documentation/.last_documented_commit` holds the last documented commit. The command leaves generated files uncommitted; the developer handles Git changes and publication outside the process.
- `docs/public/documentation_images/` holds verified captures of the current application and screenshot metadata; pages use these captures to show controls and task states.
## Background
- The package was created by [issue #69](https://github.com/heidrun-org/heidrun/issues/69). The favicon came from [issue #301](https://github.com/heidrun-org/heidrun/issues/301). The pages written by a coding agent come from [issue #375](https://github.com/heidrun-org/heidrun/issues/375).
# Directory Context: `/packages/dev_tools/documentation_updater`
## Purpose
A full npm package with two commands. `pnpm docs:update_by_ai` asks a coding agent to do a full check of the user documentation of the public website against the current rules and code, then leaves the generated files uncommitted. `pnpm docs:judge_by_ai` scores the quality of the generated pages.
## Key Exports & Entry Points
- `src/index.ts`: the public interface for another package. It exports the classes `DocumentationUpdate`, `DocumentationHints`, `DocumentationPrompt`, `DocumentationChecks`, `DocumentationGit`, and `DocumentationPaths`, and their types.
- `src/cli.ts` and `src/judge_cli.ts`: the two command lines, and the executables `documentation_updater` and `documentation_judge` of the `bin` entry in `package.json`.
- `src/documentation_judge.ts`: the class `DocumentationJudge`, which scores the pages with a rubric. `src/documentation_measures.ts` gives the mechanical measures.
- `src/documentation_update.ts`: the class `DocumentationUpdate`, which runs the steps in order.
- `src/documentation_hints.ts`: the class `DocumentationHints`, which collects the hints with no coding agent.
- `src/documentation_checks.ts`: the class `DocumentationChecks`, which tests the generated pages. The Vitest tests also run it on the real repository.
- `src/documentation_paths.ts`: the class `DocumentationPaths`, the only place that knows the paths, the mark, and the source comment.
- `tests/`: the Vitest tests. `tests/test_repository.ts` creates temporary Git repositories, and only the tests import it.
- Commands to run this folder: `pnpm docs:update_by_ai --help` and `pnpm docs:judge_by_ai --help`
- Command to test this folder: `pnpm --filter documentation_updater test`
## Rules
- The shared writer style in `src/documentation_prompt.ts` asks for focused pages, numbered task steps, control locations, expected results or checks, explained terms, consistent names, useful links, and details and solutions supported by the sources.
- Every run has two passes of the coding agent: the outline pass plans the pages and edits no file, then the writing pass writes the pages from the outline. The outline appears in the local report.
- Every generated page has one page type of the Diátaxis framework (`tutorial`, `how-to`, `reference`, `explanation`) in a comment `<!-- page type: ... -->` after the mark, and the sidebar has one group for each type.
- Every page ends with `## Related pages` (2 to 4 links), and a how-to page ends with `## Troubleshooting` (symptom, cause, solution, check) only when the sources show a failure. A source comment may name a code file when a fact comes only from the code.
- A run without `--only` is a full check. The commits since the file `.last_documented_commit` are hints only, and the first run has no hint.
- The source of truth is, in this order: the rules in `docs/agents_rules/user_interface` and the glossary, then the code, then the pull requests and the issues.
- The command writes `.last_documented_commit`, never the coding agent, and it writes the current commit of the start of the run.
- Every Markdown page of the documentation folder has the mark `<!-- generated by docs:update_by_ai -->`, except `shortcuts.md`, which `pnpm docs:shortcuts` generates.
- Every comment `<!-- source: <path> -->` names a file that exists.
- A limited run checks new or changed pages and pages naming the selected rule files, and leaves unrelated existing pages unchanged.
- Existing local changes are allowed; the coding agent preserves changes outside the files allowed by the task.
- Only a merged pull request counts as a hint: a commit whose first line starts with `Merge pull request #`. The command takes the range and the Git commands from `ChangeLogGit` of the package `change_log_generator`.
- Git history is read only; the command and coding agent never stage files, create or switch branches, write commits, push, merge, or create a pull request or merge request, because the developer handles those actions outside this process.
- The writer reuses verified screenshots from `packages/auxiliary/website_public/docs/public/documentation_images` near relevant tasks or controls, with descriptive alternative text, and never invents screenshots or image paths.
- The default coding agent is `codex`. The options `--model` and `--effort` go to the coding agent; without them, it uses its own settings. The option `--only <path...>` limits a run to the features of some rule files, and a limited run never writes `.last_documented_commit`, because the check is not full.
- Only `src/documentation_agent.ts` imports the package `raw_coding_agent_cli`.
- The judge edits no file, and its default coding agent is `claude`, so it differs from the default writer `codex`. Its answer is JSON, checked with the Zod schema `JUDGE_ANSWER_SCHEMA`.
## Background
- The package was created by [issue #375](https://github.com/heidrun-org/heidrun/issues/375).
- The coding agent needs the permission to edit files, which comes from the option `isEditAllowed` of `raw_coding_agent_cli`.
# Browse and open project files
<!-- generated by docs:update_by_ai -->
<!-- page type: how-to -->
Find a file in the selected workspace and view the file in the large Git window.
## Open a project file
<!-- source: docs/agents_rules/user_interface/sidebars/files.md -->
<!-- source: docs/agents_rules/glossary.md -->
A workspace is a project folder. The Files sidebar section shows the folder tree of the selected workspace's Git repository.
1. Select the workspace whose files you want to browse.
2. Click **Files**, the first folder icon in the sidebar icon bar of the left sidebar, above **Scripts**.
3. Click a folder row to unfold the folder.
4. Click the file row you want to open.
![Files sidebar section showing header buttons, folder rows, and file rows.](/documentation_images/files/files_sidebar.png)
The file row becomes selected, and the file opens in the large Git window. A file with no changes appears as a whole file.
## Refresh the folder tree
<!-- source: docs/agents_rules/user_interface/sidebars/files.md -->
1. Click **Refresh**, the circular arrow in the header of the Files sidebar section.
2. Check the folder tree for the updated rows.
Refresh reads the folder tree again. Newly created empty folders that have been removed outside Heidrun disappear from the folder tree after refresh.
## Troubleshooting
<!-- source: docs/agents_rules/user_interface/sidebars/files.md -->
<!-- source: packages/apps/web_frontend/src/components/FilesPanel.vue -->
<!-- source: packages/apps/web_frontend/src/i18n/locales/en/filesPanel.json -->
### “Select a workspace.” appears
**Cause**: No workspace is selected.
**Solution**:
1. Select the workspace whose files you want to browse.
**Check**: The Files sidebar section shows the folder tree when the selected workspace is a Git repository.
### “This workspace is not a Git repository.” appears
**Cause**: The selected workspace is not a Git repository.
**Solution**:
1. Select a workspace that contains a Git repository.
**Check**: The Files sidebar section shows the repository's folder tree.
### Refresh is disabled
**Cause**: The folder tree is loading.
**Solution**:
1. Wait for the folder tree to finish loading.
**Check**: **Refresh** becomes available again.
### Diff and Side by side are disabled
**Cause**: The opened file has no changes to compare.
**Solution**:
1. View the whole file already shown in the large Git window.
**Check**: The large Git window shows the file's contents; **Diff** and **Side by side** remain disabled for the unchanged file.
## Related pages
- [Create a file or folder](/documentation/create_a_file_or_folder): to add an empty file or folder in the intended location.
- [Copy a file path](/documentation/copy_a_file_path): to use a file path outside Heidrun.
- [Files sidebar section controls](/documentation/files_sidebar_section_controls): to look up buttons and folder tree indicators.
# Create a file or folder
<!-- generated by docs:update_by_ai -->
<!-- page type: how-to -->
Create an empty file or folder in the intended location of the selected repository.
## Choose the destination
<!-- source: docs/agents_rules/user_interface/sidebars/files.md -->
<!-- source: docs/agents_rules/glossary.md -->
1. Select the workspace, the project folder that contains the repository.
2. Click **Files**, the first folder icon in the sidebar icon bar of the left sidebar.
3. Select the destination using one of the actions below.
| Destination | Action |
| --- | --- |
| Inside a folder | Click the folder row to select the folder. |
| Beside an existing file | Click the file row to select the file; creation uses the folder containing the file. |
| At the repository root, outside any subfolder | Click empty space outside all rows in the Files sidebar section to clear the selection. |
## Create the file or folder
<!-- source: docs/agents_rules/user_interface/sidebars/files.md -->
1. Click **New file**, the file icon with a plus sign, or **New folder**, the folder icon with a plus sign, in the header of the Files sidebar section.
2. Type only the new name in the name box shown as the first child of the destination folder.
3. Press **Enter**.
![New file name box inside the selected docs folder, with example.md entered.](/documentation_images/files/new_file.png)
The new empty file or folder becomes the selected row. A new file also opens in the large Git window.
## Cancel creation
<!-- source: docs/agents_rules/user_interface/sidebars/files.md -->
1. Press **Escape** while the name box is open, or click outside the name box.
The name box closes without creating a file or folder.
## Troubleshooting
<!-- source: docs/agents_rules/user_interface/sidebars/files.md -->
<!-- source: packages/apps/web_frontend/src/i18n/locales/en/filesPanel.json -->
### The name box stays open and an error says the name already exists
**Cause**: A file or folder with the entered name already exists in the destination folder.
**Solution**:
1. Replace the entered name with a name that is not already used in the destination folder.
2. Press **Enter**.
**Check**: The name box closes and the new file or folder becomes the selected row.
### “A name cannot contain the character /. Select a folder first.” appears
**Cause**: The entered name contains `/` instead of being only a file or folder name.
**Solution**:
1. Press **Escape** to cancel the name box.
2. Select the destination folder in the folder tree.
3. Click **New file** or **New folder** in the header.
4. Enter a name without `/`.
5. Press **Enter**.
**Check**: The new file or folder becomes the selected row inside the destination folder.
## Related pages
- [Browse and open project files](/documentation/browse_project_files): to find the destination folder or view a file.
- [Copy a file path](/documentation/copy_a_file_path): to copy the path of the new file.
- [Files sidebar section controls](/documentation/files_sidebar_section_controls): to look up which folders remain visible.
# Copy a file path
<!-- generated by docs:update_by_ai -->
<!-- page type: how-to -->
Copy an absolute file path or a file path relative to the workspace folder.
## Copy the path
<!-- source: docs/agents_rules/user_interface/sidebars/files.md -->
<!-- source: docs/agents_rules/glossary.md -->
1. Select the workspace, the project folder containing the file.
2. Click **Files**, the first folder icon in the sidebar icon bar of the left sidebar.
3. Unfold the folders containing the file.
4. Right-click the file row to open the context menu, a small menu of actions for the file.
5. Choose **Copy absolute path** for the full path, or **Copy relative path** for the path starting from the workspace folder.
6. Check the copied text shown in the notification.
![Context menu for docs/README.md showing Copy absolute path and Copy relative path.](/documentation_images/files/copy_path.png)
The selected path is copied, and the context menu closes.
## Troubleshooting
<!-- source: docs/agents_rules/user_interface/sidebars/files.md -->
### The path-copy menu does not appear when a folder row is right-clicked
**Cause**: The path-copy context menu is available only for file rows.
**Solution**:
1. Click the folder row to unfold the folder if necessary.
2. Right-click a file row inside the folder.
**Check**: The context menu shows **Copy absolute path** and **Copy relative path**.
## Related pages
- [Browse and open project files](/documentation/browse_project_files): to find the file whose path you need.
- [Create a file or folder](/documentation/create_a_file_or_folder): to add a file before copying the file path.
- [Files sidebar section controls](/documentation/files_sidebar_section_controls): to compare the two path choices.
# Files sidebar section controls
<!-- generated by docs:update_by_ai -->
<!-- page type: reference -->
Look up the controls, appearance choices, and row indicators of the Files sidebar section.
## Header buttons
<!-- source: docs/agents_rules/user_interface/sidebars/files.md -->
<!-- source: packages/apps/web_frontend/src/components/FilesPanel.vue -->
The header stays at the top while the rows scroll. The five buttons show only icons, in this order from left to right.
| Button | Icon | Purpose |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **New file** | File with a plus sign | Opens a name box for an empty file in the selected destination. |
| **New folder** | Folder with a plus sign | Opens a name box for an empty folder in the selected destination. |
| **Refresh** | Circular arrow | Reads the folder tree again; disabled while the folder tree loads. |
| **Collapse all folders** | Square with a minus sign | Folds every folder. |
| **More options** | Three vertical dots | Opens the appearance choices for the folder tree. |
There is no button to unfold every folder.
## More options
<!-- source: docs/agents_rules/user_interface/sidebars/files.md -->
A check mark identifies the active choice in each group. The appearance choices are saved.
| Group | Choices | Meaning |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Indentation** | **Small**, **Medium**, **Large** | The horizontal space added for each folder level. |
| **Row height** | **Compact**, **Comfortable** | The vertical space occupied by each row. |
| **Indent guides** | **Show**, **Hide** | Whether lines mark the folder levels. |
![More options menu showing Indentation, Row height, and Indent guides choices.](/documentation_images/files/more_options.png)
## File context menu
<!-- source: docs/agents_rules/user_interface/sidebars/files.md -->
<!-- source: docs/agents_rules/glossary.md -->
A context menu is a small menu of actions for a row. The file context menu opens on a right-click on a file row; folder rows have no path-copy context menu.
| Item | Copied text |
| --- | --- |
| **Copy absolute path** | The full path of the file. |
| **Copy relative path** | The path of the file relative to the workspace folder. |
A notification shows the copied text. **Escape**, a click outside the context menu, or a click on an item closes the context menu.
## Folder tree indicators
<!-- source: docs/agents_rules/user_interface/sidebars/files.md -->
<!-- source: packages/apps/web_frontend/src/components/FilesPanel.vue -->
<!-- source: packages/apps/desktop_tauri/src/files.rs -->
Folders appear before files, with each group in alphabetical order. Files and folders at the same level have aligned names.
| Indicator | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| Right-pointing folder arrow | The folder is folded. |
| Downward-pointing folder arrow | The folder is unfolded. |
| Row with a blue outline and a darker background than the row under the pointer | The selected file or folder; only one row is selected. |
| Grey folder icon | A folder. |
| Grey file-kind icon | The kind of file. |
| **M** | A modified file. |
| **A** | An added file. |
| **D** | A deleted file. |
| **R** | A renamed file. |
| **U** | A new file that Git does not track yet. |
| Dot on a folder row | Changes exist inside the folder. |
Changed-file letters appear at the right of the file row.
## Visibility and remembered choices
<!-- source: docs/agents_rules/user_interface/sidebars/files.md -->
<!-- source: docs/agents_rules/glossary.md -->
<!-- source: packages/apps/web_frontend/src/i18n/locales/en/filesPanel.json -->
The Files sidebar section shows the folder tree of the selected workspace's Git repository. A workspace is a project folder.
| Choice or limit | Behaviour |
| --- | --- |
| Selected row | Each workspace keeps a separate selection. Returning to a workspace restores the selected row with the folders above the row unfolded. |
| Closing the large Git window | The selected row remains selected. |
| Changing the sidebar section | The selected row and the folded or unfolded state of folders are retained. |
| Ignored folders | Folders excluded by `.gitignore` appear only when the option to show ignored files is on. These folders cannot unfold. |
| Newly created empty folders | These folders are remembered until Heidrun restarts. A remembered folder that has been removed outside Heidrun disappears when the folder tree is read again. |
| Long file lists | “The list is too long: only the first files are shown.” means only part of the list appears. |
## Related pages
- [Browse and open project files](/documentation/browse_project_files): to find and view a file.
- [Create a file or folder](/documentation/create_a_file_or_folder): to choose a destination and create an empty file or folder.
- [Copy a file path](/documentation/copy_a_file_path): to copy either form of a file path.
