-The Files sidebar section shows the folder tree of the selected workspace's Git repository. A workspace is a project folder.
+The Files sidebar section uses the selected repository's file list.
-| Choice or limit | Behaviour |
+| Item | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| Selected row | Each workspace keeps a separate selection. Returning to a workspace restores the selected row with the folders above the row unfolded. |
| Closing the large Git window | The selected row remains selected. |
| Changing the sidebar section | The selected row and the folded or unfolded state of folders are retained. |
-| Ignored folders | Folders excluded by `.gitignore` appear only when the option to show ignored files is on. These folders cannot unfold. |
-| Newly created empty folders | These folders are remembered until Heidrun restarts. A remembered folder that has been removed outside Heidrun disappears when the folder tree is read again. |
-| Long file lists | “The list is too long: only the first files are shown.” means only part of the list appears. |
+| **Ignored files** | The checkbox below the file-name search field in the **Files** view on the left of the Files window. The choice is saved and also affects the Files sidebar section. Folders excluded by `.gitignore` appear when the checkbox is selected, but cannot unfold. |
+| Newly created empty folders | Visible only until Heidrun restarts; see [Create a file or folder](/documentation/create_a_file_or_folder#create-the-file-or-folder) for the distinction between a tree entry and a folder on disk. |
+| Long file lists | The repository list is cut to the first 50,000 entries. The warning “The list is too long: only the first files are shown.” identifies this limitation; see [Browse and open project files](/documentation/browse_project_files#long-file-lists). |
