# Browse and open project files
<!-- generated by docs:update_by_ai -->
<!-- page type: how-to -->
Find a file in the selected workspace and view the file in the large Git window.
## Select an existing workspace
<!-- source: docs/agents_rules/user_interface/workspaces_tabs_and_panes/workspace.md -->
<!-- source: docs/agents_rules/glossary.md -->
<!-- source: packages/apps/web_frontend/src/components/WorkspaceStatusSummary.vue -->
A workspace is a project folder. Choose a workspace that contains a Git repository.
1. Click the workspace name at the bottom-left of the application to open its information card, a small card with details and a list of workspaces.
2. Click the workspace you want in the list below the details.
The information card closes, and the workspace name at the bottom-left changes to the selected workspace.
## Open a project file
<!-- source: docs/agents_rules/user_interface/sidebars/files.md -->
<!-- source: docs/agents_rules/glossary.md -->
<!-- source: packages/apps/web_frontend/src/components/GitModal.vue -->
<!-- source: packages/apps/web_frontend/src/i18n/locales/en/gitModal.json -->
<!-- source: packages/apps/web_frontend/src/stores/files.ts -->
The Files sidebar section shows the folder tree of the selected workspace's Git repository.
1. Click **Files**, the first folder icon in the sidebar icon bar, the narrow vertical bar at the outer edge of the left sidebar, above **Scripts**.
2. Click a folder row to unfold the folder.
3. Click the file row you want to open.
The file row becomes selected, and the large Git window opens over the application to show the file. An unchanged file appears as a whole file; **Diff** and **Side by side** are disabled because there are no changes to compare.
4. Press **Escape** or click **Close**, the cross at the top-right of the large Git window, to return to the sidebar.
The file row remains selected. This example shows `docs` unfolded and `docs/README.md` selected after the large Git window has been closed; the large Git window is not visible in the screenshot.
![Files sidebar section with docs unfolded and docs/README.md selected after the large Git window was closed.](/documentation_images/files/files_sidebar.png)
The yellow dot beside `.pnpm-store` means that the folder contains changes.
## Refresh the folder tree
<!-- source: docs/agents_rules/user_interface/sidebars/files.md -->
Use **Refresh** when a file or folder was added or removed outside Heidrun and the folder tree still shows the old list.
1. Click **Refresh**, the circular arrow in the header of the Files sidebar section.
2. Unfold the folder where the change was made.
Check that an added file now appears or a removed file no longer appears. Refresh also removes the tree entry for a remembered empty folder that no longer exists on disk.
## Long file lists
<!-- source: packages/apps/desktop_tauri/src/files.rs -->
<!-- source: packages/apps/web_frontend/src/components/FilesPanel.vue -->
<!-- source: packages/apps/web_frontend/src/i18n/locales/en/filesPanel.json -->
<!-- source: packages/apps/web_frontend/src/components/FilesModal.vue -->
<!-- source: packages/apps/web_frontend/src/stores/files.ts -->
“The list is too long: only the first files are shown.” means the repository list was cut to the first 50,000 entries. Files beyond that limit are missing from the folder tree, and the Files window's search by name uses the same limited list. There is no control to load the remaining entries.
